# enclave ggml wasi-nn backend - GGUF language models (llama.cpp) behind the
# standard wasi:nn interface, against wasmtime v45.0.0.
#
# APPLY ORDER: LAST, after wasmtime-onnx-gpu-strict.patch (this diff is based
# on a tree with the other enclave patches applied - both touch
# crates/wasi-nn/Cargo.toml and backend/mod.rs).
#
# What it adds: crates/wasi-nn/src/backend/ggml.rs (a backend that binds the
# system-linked enclave_llama shim - see wasm/llama-shim/), its registration
# in backend/mod.rs + wit.rs FromStr ("ggml" now parses for -S nn-graph), a
# no-dependency `ggml` cargo feature, build.rs link directives driven by
# ELL_LIB_LOCATION (same system-link pattern as ORT_LIB_LOCATION), and the
# serve-startup preload hoist (serve.rs + wasi-nn lib.rs/in_memory.rs, below).
# The ggml backend adds NO crates (pure std + FFI); the Cargo.lock hunk only
# records the other patches' deps (half, sha2).
#
# Model delivery: -S nn-graph=ggml::<dir> preloads <dir>/model.gguf (or the
# single *.gguf, or part 00001 of ONE complete "<prefix>-NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf"
# split family - HF's 50GB per-file cap forces big models to ship split, and
# llama.cpp derives the sibling paths from part 00001's file name) under the
# DIRECTORY BASENAME; guests load_by_name() it, so
# weights never transit the guest's 32-bit linear memory - model size is
# bounded by the tenant's share, not wasm32. The model loads ONCE per
# process, AT SERVER STARTUP: upstream `wasmtime serve` preloads -S nn-graph
# inside new_store(), i.e. per request store (wasip2 components get a fresh
# store per request), which would pull a multi-GB GGUF into VRAM on every
# request and free it after. This patch hoists the preload to right after
# the listener binds (weights hit VRAM the moment the deployment is up;
# connections arriving during the load queue in the listen backlog) and
# shares the graphs with every store through Arc'd registry clones
# (InMemoryRegistry gains Clone, lib.rs gains preload_registry()). A graph
# that fails to preload (typically CUDA OOM: the share cannot hold it) is
# SKIPPED loudly instead of killing the server: the deployment serves the
# graphs that did fit, and a guest load_by_name() of a skipped graph errors
# per-model. The wasm-manager emits ggml graphs SMALLEST-FIRST, so what fits
# is deterministic (residency is first-come-first-served within the share)
# and one published app scales with the deployment's resources - llm-chat's
# smallest-first warmup ladder + unfit-model reporting ride on this.
# Contract: input "tokens" I32 [1,n] -> output "logits" Fp32 [1,n_vocab].
# VISION: a volume that pairs its model with an *mmproj*.gguf projector also
# accepts input "image" U8 [n] = one image FILE's bytes -> output "image_pos"
# I32 [1], the positions it consumed; guests interleave it with "tokens" to
# place a picture inside a rendered prompt, and "caps" gained a fourth element
# (vision) so they can tell before they try. All the model-specific vision
# work (marker tokens, non-causal image masks, M-RoPE image positions) lives
# in libmtmd behind the shim's ell_mtmd_* entry points, which this backend
# resolves by DLSYM rather than linking: a node whose toolchain tarball
# predates them builds and serves exactly as before and reports vision=0, so
# turning vision on is a toolchain bump, never a rebuild requirement. The
# projector is loaded LAZILY, on the first image, so text-only deployments
# never pay its VRAM. A volume's projector is also what keeps its second gguf
# from confusing the model pick (is_mmproj_name).
# CONTINUOUS BATCHING: each graph has ONE shared llama context (created on
# first use) with a unified KV pool of N_CTX tokens total; a wasi-nn
# execution context is a SEQUENCE HANDLE into it (per-request cost = a seq
# slot, not a context allocation), and concurrent requests' decode steps
# merge into single llama_decode calls (leader protocol in GgmlServer).
# GGUF volumes must also carry tokenizer.json (guest-side tokenization).
#
# GPU: the llama.cpp libs are GGML_BACKEND_DL builds - the cpu/cuda compute
# backends are dlopened MODULES, loaded by the shim's ell_init() from
# ENCLAVE_GGML_BACKEND_DIR. The wasmtime binary therefore carries NO
# DT_NEEDED on libcuda.so.1 (driver libs exist only where the nvidia
# container runtime injects them - never on CPU-flavor nodes). STRICT GPU:
# offload requested (ENCLAVE_GGML_N_GPU_LAYERS != 0) + no ggml GPU device
# loaded = loud load failure, never a silent CPU fallback. The preload
# registry hardcodes ExecutionTarget::Cpu, so the env is ALSO what turns
# offload on for preloaded graphs (the wasm-manager sets -1 per GPU tenant).
#
# Tuning env (host process only): ENCLAVE_GGML_N_CTX (default 8192 - the
# SHARED pool size in tokens, not a per-request window),
# ENCLAVE_GGML_N_BATCH (512), ENCLAVE_GGML_N_GPU_LAYERS (-1 = offload all),
# ENCLAVE_GGML_MAX_SESSIONS (default 1 - concurrent sequences per graph;
# slots share the ONE pool so raising it costs no extra pre-allocated VRAM;
# no free slot = fail-fast [sessions_busy] for guests to wait-and-retry on,
# pool pressure at decode = retryable [kv_pool_full]),
# ENCLAVE_GGML_BACKEND_DIR (backend-module dir; unset = exe dir + cwd).
# Vision-only knobs: ENCLAVE_GGML_IMAGE_MAX_TOKENS (cap the tokens ONE image
# may expand to on dynamic-resolution models; 0 = the mmproj's metadata),
# ENCLAVE_GGML_MMPROJ_FILE (projector name when it is not *mmproj*.gguf),
# ENCLAVE_GGML_MTMD_THREADS (preprocessing threads, default 4), and
# ENCLAVE_GGML_N_UBATCH - read by the SHIM, and needed only by models that
# decode images with a non-causal mask, which must hold a whole image in one
# physical batch ([image_too_wide] otherwise).
#
# Build: cargo build --release --features "wasi-nn,wasmtime-wasi-nn/ggml"
# with ELL_LIB_LOCATION=<dir holding libenclave_llama.so + libllama.so>
# (the enclave-llamacpp toolchain artifact; llamacpp-toolchain.yml builds it).
# CPU-smoked 2026-07-07 on the fully-patched tree (qwen2.5-0.5b q4_k_m,
# ~114 tok/s via the dlopened cpu module; self-deterministic; strict-GPU
# guard + no-backend failure paths exercised). NOTE: greedy token streams
# differ between GGML_NATIVE=ON and =OFF kernel builds (near-tie argmax
# flips) - compare like with like when validating determinism. Split-family
# smoke 2026-07-09: a q4_k_m gguf-split into 3 parts loads through the staged
# symlink dir and greedy-decodes TOKEN-IDENTICAL to the merged file.
#
# 2026-08-01 topk prefilter: an optional {"topk": K} input beside "tokens"
# makes every logits return sparse - "topk_ids" I32 [n,K] + "topk_logits"
# Fp32 [n,K], host-side selection, rows sorted descending. Motivated by the
# speculative-decoding round-cost measurement (~90-120ms per verify round,
# dominated by (k+1) full-vocab rows crossing the guest boundary + wasm
# scans); also trims the per-token tax of plain decode. Guests sniff the
# output name and fall back to dense "logits" on engines without it.
#
# 2026-08-01 timing verb: {"timing": 1} beside any verb appends "elapsed_us"
# I32 [1] (wall time of the whole compute call, lock waits included) to the
# outputs. The per-verb instrument that replaced guessing at the speculative
# round-cost decomposition; costs one Instant::now when unused.
